# cmd.exe tolerates LF in most of a batch file but mis-parses labels and the
# final line without CRLF, so the launcher is pinned to CRLF wherever it is
# checked out or unzipped. The shell launcher needs the opposite guarantee.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# The tracked model. Git's own binary detection already spares it from the
# CRLF conversion core.autocrlf=true would otherwise apply, but "already
# spares it" is a heuristic and the failure it guards against is a pickle that
# unpickles into a traceback on someone else's machine. Say it outright.
*.pkl binary
